  70:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h **** /**
  71:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * @addtogroup CCU8
  72:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
  73:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * @brief Capture Compare Unit 8 (CCU8) low level driver for XMC family of microcontrollers<br>
  74:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
  75:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * The CCU8 peripheral functions play a major role in applications that need complex Pulse Width Mo
  76:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * generation, with complementary high side and low side switches, multi phase control. These funct
  77:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * with a very flexible and programmable signal conditioning scheme, make the CCU8 the must have pe
  78:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * of the art motor control, multi phase and multi level power electronics systems.\n
  79:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * Each CCU8 module is comprised of four identical 16 bit Capture/Compare Timer slices, CC8y (where
  80:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * timer slice can work in compare mode or in capture mode.
  81:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
  82:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * APIs provided in this file cover the following functional blocks of CCU8:\n
  83:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -- Timer configuration, Capture configuration, Function/Event configuration, Interrupt configura
  84:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * \par Note:
  85:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * 1. SLICE (APIs prefixed with e.g. XMC_CCU8_SLICE_)\n
  86:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * 2. Module (APIs are not having any prefix e.g. XMC_CCU8_) \n
  87:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
  88:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * \par Timer(Compare mode) configuration:\n
  89:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * This section of the LLD provides the configuration structure XMC_CCU8_SLICE_COMPARE_CONFIG_t, 
  90:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * XMC_CCU8_SLICE_DEAD_TIME_CONFIG_t and the initialization functions XMC_CCU8_SLICE_CompareInit(),
  91:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
  92:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * It can be used to:
  93:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# Start and Stop the timer. (XMC_CCU8_SLICE_StartTimer(), XMC_CCU8_SLICE_StopTimer())
  94:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# Update the period, compare, Dither, Prescaler  and Passive values. (XMC_CCU8_SLICE_SetTimerPe
  95:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *    XMC_CCU8_SLICE_SetTimerCompareMatch(), XMC_CCU8_SLICE_SetPrescaler(), XMC_CCU8_SLICE_SetDithe
  96:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *    XMC_CCU8_SLICE_SetPassiveLevel())
  97:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# Configure the dead time.(XMC_CCU8_SLICE_SetDeadTimeValue(), XMC_CCU8_SLICE_SetDeadTimePrescal
  98:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# Enable the slices to support multichannel mode. (XMC_CCU8_SLICE_EnableMultiChannelMode())
  99:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * 
 100:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * \par Capture configuration:\n
 101:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * This section of the LLD provides the configuration structure XMC_CCU8_SLICE_CAPTURE_CONFIG_t and
 102:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * function XMC_CCU8_SLICE_CaptureInit().\n
 103:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
 104:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * It can be used to:
 105:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# Configure the capture functionality. (XMC_CCU8_SLICE_Capture0Config(), XMC_CCU8_SLICE_Capture
 106:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# Read the captured values along with the status, which indicate the value is latest or not.
 107:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *    (XMC_CCU8_SLICE_GetCaptureRegisterValue())
 108:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * 
 109:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * \par Function/Event configuration:\n
 110:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * This section of the LLD provides the configuration structure XMC_CCU8_SLICE_EVENT_CONFIG_t.\n
 111:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * 
 112:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * It can be used to:
 113:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# Enable and Disable the events. (XMC_CCU8_SLICE_EnableEvent(), XMC_CCU8_SLICE_DisableEvent())
 114:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# Configure to start and stop the timer on external events.(XMC_CCU8_SLICE_StartConfig(), XMC_C
 115:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# Modulation, external load and Gating of the timer output.(XMC_CCU8_SLICE_ModulationConfig(), 
 116:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *    XMC_CCU8_SLICE_LoadConfig(), XMC_CCU8_SLICE_GateConfig())
 117:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# Control the count direction of the timer based on the external event. (XMC_CCU8_SLICE_Directi
 118:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# Count the external events.(XMC_CCU8_SLICE_CountConfig())
 119:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * -# External Trap. Which can be used as protective feature.(XMC_CCU8_SLICE_EnableTrap(), XMC_CCU8
 120:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *    XMC_CCU8_SLICE_TrapConfig())
 121:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
 122:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * \par Interrupt configuration:\n
 123:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * This section of the LLD provides the function to configure the interrupt node to each event (XMC
 124:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
 125:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * @{
