1680:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
1681:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * \par<b>Description:</b><br>
1682:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * Retrieves the timer period value currently effective, by reading CC8yPR register.\n\n
1683:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * If the timer is active then the value being returned is currently being used for the PWM period.
1684:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
1685:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * \par<b>Note:</b><br>
1686:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * The XMC_CCU8_SLICE_SetTimerPeriodMatch() would set the new period value to a shadow register.
1687:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * This would only transfer the new values into the actual period register if the shadow transfer r
1688:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * is enabled and if a period match occurs. Hence a consecutive call to XMC_CCU8_SLICE_GetTimerPeri
1689:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * would not reflect the new values until the shadow transfer completes.
1690:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
1691:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * \par<b>Related APIs:</b><br>
1692:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *  XMC_CCU8_SLICE_SetTimerPeriodMatch().
1693:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  */
