1729:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * Retrieves the timer compare value currently effective, by reading CC8yCR1S and CC8yCR2S register
1730:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * If the timer is active then the value being returned is currently being for the PWM duty cycle( 
1731:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  *
1732:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * \par<b>Note:</b><br>
1733:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * The XMC_CCU8_SLICE_SetTimerCompareMatch() would set the new compare value to a shadow register.
1734:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * This would only transfer the new values into the actual compare register if the shadow transfer 
1735:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * is enabled and if a period match occurs. Hence a consecutive call to XMC_CCU8_SLICE_GetTimerComp
1736:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_ccu8.h ****  * would not reflect the new values until the shadow transfer completes.
